e S  ones details hinted outies motorsport  pedigree like the stainless steel pedal  caps and the leather trim flat-bottom  steering wheel the s1 is fitted with a  6-speed manual transmission and there's  no overlooking the fact that this cars a  Quattro  sport seats with integrated headrests  kakuhen the driver and front seat  passenger giving them the feeling of  being in a real race car but open the  trunk and you'll see that there's not  much luggage space it's one of the s  ones minor weaknesses  so what's mattis's overall impression he  says the s1 is great fun to drive it  doesn't have a big trunk or a lot of  room in the backseat but he says these  aren't must-haves for a fun hot hatch  but that fun does come at a price in  Germany the s-1 has a starting price of  close to thirty one thousand euros  thirteen thousand more than a bare-bones  a1 sportback
 

